@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# Development Runtime Governor
+
+This document describes the tenth data/runtime rewrite slice for `enn_torch_dev`.
+
+## Goal
+
+`BudgetedBatcher` applies a static pre-execution `BatchBudget`, and
+`RuntimeRetryRunner` handles side-effect-safe OOM retry after `RuntimeStep` returns
+`StepResult` objects. This slice adds a conservative observation layer that adjusts
+future budgets from already-produced results:
+
+```text
+KVBatch stream
+  -> BudgetedBatcher(current_budget)
+  -> RuntimeRetryRunner
+  -> RuntimeStep.run(batch)
+  -> StepResult stream
+  -> ConservativeRuntimeGovernor.observe_results(...)
+  -> next BatchBudget
+```
+
+The governor does not run a model, catch exceptions, split batches, own retry, or
+probe costs directly. It only observes `StepResult` streams and updates a stored
+`BatchBudget` using static conservative rules.
+
+## Contract
+
+A configured budget field is a `BatchBudget` field whose value is not `None`.
+The governor only adjusts configured fields and never activates a `None` field.
+
+`GovernorPolicy` owns static bounds and scaling rules:
+
+- `shrink_factor`: multiplicative decrease applied to all configured budget
+  fields after any `StepStatus.OOM_FAULT` result;
+- `grow_factor`: multiplicative increase applied to all configured budget fields
+  after a success streak;
+- `grow_after_successes`: number of all-success observations required before
+  growth;
+- `min_items`, `max_items`, `min_host_bytes`, `max_host_bytes`,
+  `min_device_bytes`, and `max_device_bytes`: optional positive lower/upper
+  bounds for future `BatchBudget` values.
+
+Shrink uses `floor(current * shrink_factor)` and grow uses
+`ceil(current * grow_factor)`. Values are clamped to the configured bounds and
+never reduced below 1 for configured fields.
+
+`RuntimeGovernorState` stores the current budget and streak counters. It is an
+immutable state object; `ConservativeRuntimeGovernor` replaces `self.state` with a
+new state after each observation.
+
+`ConservativeRuntimeGovernor` exposes:
+
+- `current_budget` for the active budget;
+- `observe_results(results)` to consume an iterable of `StepResult` objects,
+  update the active budget, and return a `GovernorDecision`.
+
+`GovernorDecision` records the previous and next budgets, observed statuses,
+consecutive success/OOM counters, a reason string, and peak resource values
+reported by attached `ResourceSample` objects.
+
+## Decision Rules
+
+For each `observe_results(...)` call:
+
+1. empty result streams keep the current budget unchanged;
+2. any `StepStatus.OOM_FAULT` shrinks configured budget fields and resets the
+   success streak, even when successes or non-OOM faults are mixed in;
+3. all-success observations increment the success streak by one per observe call,
+   not by result count;
+4. reaching `grow_after_successes` grows the budget once and resets the success
+   streak to zero;
+5. non-OOM faults keep the budget unchanged and reset success/OOM streaks;
+6. lower and upper bounds are always respected, but only for fields already
+   configured on the active budget;
+7. resource samples are recorded in the decision and reason text, but they do not
+   drive automatic tuning beyond the static rules in this slice.
+
+## Relationship to Retry and Batching
+
+`BudgetedBatcher` remains the static gate that applies the current budget to
+incoming `KVBatch` objects.
+
+`RuntimeRetryRunner` remains the side-effect-safe post-execution OOM retry
+boundary.
+
+`ConservativeRuntimeGovernor` observes the resulting `StepResult` stream and
+produces the next budget for a future pass. It should not be folded into either
+`BudgetedBatcher` or `RuntimeRetryRunner`.
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- AutoGovernor full implementation.
+- Learned or model-specific tuning.
+- Persistent calibration cache or history database.
+- ResourceMonitor feedback loops beyond recording observed peaks.
+- ModelCostProbe-driven policy changes.
+- SPDL queue-depth tuning.
+- Device transfer.
+- AMP or precision fallback.
+- Optimizer rollback or training semantic recovery.
+- Distributed coordination.
+
+## Test Commands
+
+```bash
+python -m pytest enn_torch_dev/debug/runtime/test_runtime_governor.py -q
+python -m pytest enn_torch_dev/debug/runtime/test_runtime_retry.py -q
+python -m pytest enn_torch_dev/debug/runtime/test_budgeted_batcher.py -q
+python -m pytest enn_torch_dev/debug/runtime -q
+python -m pytest enn_torch_dev/debug/data -q
+python -m pytest enn_torch_dev/debug -q
+git diff --check
+```
+
+## Next Step
+
+A later slice can wire this governor into a higher-level orchestration loop that
+feeds each `GovernorDecision.next_budget` back into `BudgetedBatcher`. That loop
+should remain conservative and should not add persistent calibration or learned
+autotuning without a separate design decision.
